      "text": "We are given the problem \\(\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3}\\) and need to find its value. To do this, we will use the periodicity property of the sine function. \n\nThe sine function is periodic with a period of \\(2\\pi\\). This means \\(\\sin x = \\sin (x + 2k\\pi)\\) for any integer \\(k\\). We will use this property to simplify \\(\\frac{11 \\pi}{3}\\).\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\(\\frac{11 \\pi}{3}\\) by finding an equivalent angle within one period of \\(2\\pi\\). This involves finding the remainder when \\(\\frac{11 \\pi}{3}\\) is divided by \\(2\\pi\\).\n\nLet's perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{11 \\pi}{3} \\div 2\\pi = \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} \\div 2\\pi = \\frac{11 \\pi}{3 \\cdot 2\\pi} = \\frac{11 \\pi}{6\\pi} = \\frac{11}{6}\n\\]\n\nThe integer part of \\(\\frac{11}{6}\\) is 1, so we subtract \\(2\\pi\\) (which is \\(\\frac{12\\pi}{6}\\)) from \\(\\frac{11\\pi}{3}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{11 \\pi}{3} - 2\\pi = \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} - \\frac{12 \\pi}{3} = -\\frac{\\pi}{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(\\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = -\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 2\\pi\\). However, negative angles can also be simplified using their positive versions. So, we can write:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3} = \\sin \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 2\\pi\\right)\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\sin (\\pi - x) = \\sin x\\), we have:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3} + 2\\pi\\right) = \\sin \\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3} + \\frac{6\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\sin \\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)\n\\]\n\nNow, \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\) is within the range \\([0, 2\\pi)\\). We can now use the reference angle for \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\), which is \\(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} = 2\\pi - \\frac{\\pi}{3}\\). The sine of an angle in the fourth quadrant is negative, so:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\(\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{3} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\), hence:\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\sin \\frac{11 \\pi}{3}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\n\\]",
